status.h: map the sig* setjmp variants to plain setjmp/longjmp on MayteraOS.

A TARGET ADAPTATION, not a bug fix. bc-gh uses sigsetjmp(sjb, 0) / siglongjmp /
sigjmp_buf for its exception-handling non-local jumps. The MayteraOS freestanding
libc <setjmp.h> provides only setjmp/longjmp (there are no per-thread signal
masks to save). Because bc always passes savesigs = 0, sigsetjmp is exactly
equivalent to setjmp and siglongjmp to longjmp, so this mapping is behaviour-
preserving. Selected by -DMAYTERAOS in the port cflags; every other target
(including the real POSIX one) is byte-for-byte unaltered. The upstream source
already ships this identical mapping for _WIN32; this hunk adds the MayteraOS
branch beside it.
--- a/include/status.h
+++ b/include/status.h
@@ -77,6 +77,11 @@
 
 #else // _WIN32
 #define BC_FILE_SEP '/'
+#ifdef MAYTERAOS
+#define sigjmp_buf jmp_buf
+#define sigsetjmp(j, s) setjmp(j)
+#define siglongjmp longjmp
+#endif
 #endif // _WIN32
 
 #ifndef BC_ENABLED
